## Where to find it

The **Teachers** group in the side drawer, which holds an **Overview** dashboard, the **Directory**,
**Attendance** and **Substitution**. Adding, editing and viewing an individual teacher are all
reached from the Directory rather than being separate drawer items.

Creating and editing teachers is separately permissioned from simply viewing them, so plenty of
staff can browse the Directory without being able to change anything in it.

## Adding and editing a teacher

- **Directory → Add** opens a blank teacher form.
- Editing an existing teacher opens the same form pre-filled, reached from that teacher's profile.

Because it's one form either way, a field that's required when creating is required when editing —
there's no reduced "quick edit" version to look for.

## A teacher's profile

Selecting a teacher from the Directory opens their profile, which is where their individual
analytics live. From there you can drill into that specific teacher's attendance, and from that
into a **monthly** breakdown. These are proper addressable pages, so a particular teacher's
attendance view can be bookmarked or linked directly.

## Your own profile

**My Profile** is a separate top-level drawer item and is self-service — teachers use it without
needing any Teachers-section access. It covers three things:

- **Account** — your username and, if you're a teacher, your teacher ID. These are shown for
  reference, not edited here.
- **Teacher Profile** — your full name, date of birth and gender, plus optional contact number,
  email, address, religion, ethnicity and nationality. You can also set or remove a profile photo.
- **Change Password** — current password, then the new one twice.

{% callout type="note" %}
If **My Profile** appears in your drawer but opening it sends you back to the dashboard, your
account predates the permission that controls it. That's an access-configuration gap rather than a
fault with your account — ask your admin to grant it.
{% /callout %}

